Built stdlib-only compress.py supporting both requested commands, with inferred numeric-column compression and a lossless fallback. Verified byte-identical restoration of corpus.txt and additional empty, text, and binary inputs. The corpus compresses from 313,972 to 8,025 bytes—a 97.444% size reduction, beating default zlib’s 35,399 bytes. Registered the stable round-trip-checking assay as `python3 -B assay.py`.